# `homelab/topology/index.html` used to be listed here as a generated file that
# git must never merge and never diff. It is neither of those things any more:
# it is a hand-drawn page, 19 KB of SVG that somebody laid out, and its diffs
# are exactly what review should be reading. Nothing about it is derived.
#
# The delta pages below still are. They were rendered by a tool that no longer
# runs here, and they are kept only because dated changelog entries link to
# them — frozen, not maintained.
#
# -merge tells git never to attempt a textual three-way merge on them. A
# line-level merge of two 700KB rendered documents does not produce a valid
# page, it produces a broken one that still looks like HTML — the worst kind of
# conflict resolution, because it can pass review.
#
# -diff keeps them out of diffs and `git log -p`, where a re-render shows as
# thousands of changed lines that mean nothing.
homelab/changes/**/index.html    -merge -diff
homelab/changes/**/*.receipt.json -diff
